## Purpose

Make every Tool Shed installation and upgrade tell one coherent truth about what the selected
release can actually do. Correct the split-authority state from GitHub issue #66, then use the
`workpc` field migration as a durable acceptance fixture for runtime capability, failure
diagnostics, relationship preservation, semantic-operation boundaries, and complete convergence.

## Desired Outcome

Every install and supported update entry point evaluates the current workspace against the
selected release, applies all safe guarded convergence steps, and leaves either a fully enabled
workspace or one functional, explicitly limited authority mode with exact recovery actions. All
consumers agree on authority and inventory; configured runtimes prove guarded-write capability;
conversion preserves semantic state; and the result is qualified on Linux and Windows before
release and recursive outcome closure.

